# Claim

1. An oil supply structure for a planetary gear device, comprising:

a carrier-rotating tubular body configured to rotate together with a carrier of the planetary gear device, the carrier-rotating tubular body having an oil introduction port formed therein for introducing lubricating oil from an oil supply source;

a sliding annular body disposed radially outward of the carrier-rotating tubular body so as to be relatively rotatable with respect thereto, the sliding annular body having an oil supply passage formed therein, the oil supply passage being configured to communicate with the oil introduction port of the carrier-rotating tubular body so as to supply the lubricating oil to a lubrication target portion of the planetary gear device;

a pair of seal rings disposed between an outer peripheral surface of the carrier-rotating tubular body and an inner peripheral surface of the sliding annular body, the pair of seal rings being spaced apart from each other in an axial direction so as to be positioned on both axial sides of a communicating portion between the oil introduction port and the oil supply passage, thereby sealing the lubricating oil supplied through the communicating portion; and

a pressure-reducing bypass passage formed in at least one of the carrier-rotating tubular body and the sliding annular body so as to allow a portion of the lubricating oil to bypass the communicating portion between the oil introduction port and the oil supply passage, the pressure-reducing bypass passage being configured to reduce an oil pressure acting on the pair of seal rings.
